  "custom_logic_notes": "Five distinct entry algorithms selectable via Mode enum: Breakdown (oscillator crosses level 50), OscTwist (oscillator direction change via color states 1-4), SignalTwist (signal line direction change), OscDisposition (oscillator crosses signal line via disposition states), SignalBreakdown (signal line crosses level 50). The ColorStochNR custom indicator exposes 5 buffers: buffer 0=main line, buffer 1=signal line, buffer 2=oscillator color/trend state (1-4), buffer 3=signal line values, buffer 4=disposition state (1=above signal, 2=below signal). Signal logic uses previous bar [1] vs current bar [0] comparison. Entry permissions are gated by BuyPosOpen/SellPosOpen booleans; exit permissions by BuyPosClose/SellPosClose. Recount mechanism re-evaluates signals on CopyBuffer failure.",
  "external_dependencies": [
    "TradeAlgorithms.mqh"
  ],
  "estimated_difficulty": "medium",
  "backtest_data_needs": "H4",
  "python_conversion_notes": "Requires implementation of ColorStochNR stochastic indicator with noise reduction (Sens parameter) and its 5 output buffers. TradeAlgorithms.mqh must be reverse-engineered or reimplemented: BuyPositionOpen, SellPositionOpen, BuyPositionClose, SellPositionClose, GlobalVariableDel_, CIsNewBar, LoadHistory. Position sizing logic is dual-mode (negative=lot, positive=deposit fraction). The 5 entry modes are mutually exclusive and must all be ported. Signal timestamps (UpSignalTime/DnSignalTime) are used for trade identification passed to open functions. The EA uses SeriesInfoInteger for last bar date which has no direct Python equivalent — use bar timestamps instead.",
